THOUGHT: The field glideContext is currently non-nullable but is set to null in clear(), causing the NullAway ASSIGN_FIELD_NULLABLE error. Since this helper is reused and clear() resets its state, making glideContext explicitly @Nullable and updating its usages to handle null (e.g., via a local non-null check in getRewinder) will satisfy NullAway without changing behavior. I’ll (1) annotate glideContext as @Nullable, (2) adjust getRewinder to defensively handle a null glideContext by throwing an IllegalStateException, and then (3) run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '31s/^	  private GlideContext glideContext;/	  @Nullable private GlideContext glideContext;/' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/engine/DecodeHelper.java && sed -i '106,108c\	  <T> DataRewinder<T> getRewinder(T data) {
	    GlideContext localGlideContext = glideContext;
	    if (localGlideContext == null) {
	      throw new IllegalStateException("glideContext must be non-null to get a DataRewinder");
	    }
	    return localGlideContext.getRegistry().getRewinder(data);
	  }' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/engine/DecodeHelper.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -i "NullAway" -n new_build_output.log | tail -n 5
```

